public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
            System.out.println(arr[i]);
        }
    }
}
o/p-{10, 20, 30, 40, 50}


Explanation:
- Loop executes n times.
- If array size is 5, loop runs 5 times.
- If array size is 100, loop runs 100 times.
Time Complexity: O(n)
